  "term": "cannabis intoxication",
  "definition": "Cannabis intoxication is the short-term state after using cannabis in which mental and motor performance can be disrupted. In the supplied source, it is linked with poorer lateral control while driving, slower driving, slower simple reactions after inhalation, more response-inhibition errors, and reduced short-term memory.",
